        "body": "### EcoliTyper v1.4.0 Release Notes\r\n\r\nThis release adds mobile genetic element profiling, disk management controls for large cohorts, and a new browser for public genome selection. It also fixes a few issues that surfaced on large-scale runs.\r\nNew Features\r\n\r\n## MGE Profiling (mobileOG-db).\r\n\r\n Every genome now gets mobile genetic element profiling through the mobileOG-db database. Twelve columns of per-hit detail are parsed, aggregated per sample, and displayed in a dedicated interactive tab with per-lineage aggregate views.\r\n\r\n## Report-Level Disk Management.\r\n A new --report-level {final,summary,full} flag gives explicit control over intermediate output. On a 1,000-genome cohort, final keeps the run under roughly 80 MB, summary (default) retains batch summaries, and full keeps everything. A safety check prevents pruning when the final report directory is missing or empty.\r\n\r\n## ECLIPSE Browser. \r\n\r\nA new browser-based companion at https://bbeckley-hub.github.io/eclipse/ provides access to 431,592 public E. coli genomes. Users can filter by MLST, phylogroup, serotype, CH type, pathotype, AMR genes, virulence factors, country, source, host, and collection year, then export a plain-text accession list for NCBI datasets. No installation, account, or API key required.\r\n\r\n## MLST Database Management. \r\n\r\nTwo new commands mirror the StaphScope workflow. --pull-mlst-db downloads a pre-built scheme from GitHub in about two minutes with no API key. --update-mlst-db fetches the latest alleles from PubMLST in 10 to 20 minutes and requires a one-time API key.\r\n\r\n## Species Gate. \r\n\r\nFASTA QC now writes FASTA_QC_species_passed.txt. Only samples that pass the E. coli / Shigella species check proceed to downstream modules. Non-target assemblies are excluded with a logged warning, avoiding false-positive MLST, serotype, and AMR calls.\r\n\r\n## Complete Subprocess Logging.\r\n ecolityper_run.log now captures full stdout and stderr from every module without truncation. When a module fails, its complete output is echoed to the console with the traceback.\r\nImprovements\r\n\r\n## Docker image overhaul. \r\n\r\nThe image is now rebuilt on mambaorg/micromamba with a BuildKit cache mount. Compressed size drops from over 5 GB to about 1.8 GB. All databases (AMRFinderPlus, MLST Achtman, ABRicate, mobileOG-db) are baked in during build, so first-run network calls are zero. Code-only rebuilds finish in about 30 seconds.\r\n\r\n\r\n## Upgrade Notes\r\n\r\nConda users should run ecolityper --pull-mlst-db and ecolityper --update-amr-db once after upgrading. Docker and Singularity users skip this step because every database is already inside the image.\r\n\r\nFor large cohort runs on shared filesystems, add --report-level final to avoid hitting quota with intermediate files.\r\nCitation\r\n\r\nIf you use EcoliTyper or ECLIPSE in your research, please cite:\r\n\r\nBeckley B, Amarh V. EcoliTyper: a species-optimized computational pipeline for comprehensive genotyping and surveillance of Escherichia coli. BMC Bioinformatics. 2026;27:182. doi:10.1186/s12859-026-06529-6",
